      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Decreasing pain does not mean the underlying blockage is gone, and a high dose of ibuprofen can actually cause skin bruising or worsen kidney function if you are already stone-blocked. Drinking a gallon of water isn't a substitute for medical evaluation, especially because the \"heartbeat\" pulsing sensation combined with your history could indicate an infection that requires antibiotics or targeted treatment immediately. Waiting until tomorrow increases the risk of needing emergency surgery with severe bleeding or sepsis, which would make you significantly more miserable than you are now.",
